:"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nI've loaded my project which was last working in 4.4 Dev 6 into 4.4 Beta 1, where the issue occurs.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta1 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6081) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13650HX (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nParticle systems with the \"Oneshot\" setting, which are spawned into the scene with \"Emitting = false\" and gdscript enables the emitting flag, no longer play the full sequence. Disabling oneshot allows the full sequence to play.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen the attached test project and run it. You'll see the particle system only appears for a single frame before being freed. This is because the emitting property is being set to \"false\" elsewhere outside the script (the test project only has 1 script).\n\nIn previous versions, the one-shot animation would run to completion, then emitting would be set to false (presumably by code within the particle system itself).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[reproduce-oneshot-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18462604/reproduce-oneshot-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/